{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>תושיה</b> — the tav is added from יש, and wisdom is called thus because it exists and endures forever, and HaShem stores it for the upright, because they guard with it paths of justice — and they are the commandments." "<b>and He preserves the way of His devout ones</b> — HaShem, just as they [the upright] guard the paths."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:48.451774782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}